`Setup NAHPU` is a guided pass over the settings a new installation needs
before the first project: the catalog format, how field and tissue IDs are
formed, the controlled vocabularies for sites, events, and specimens, and the
bundled export presets.

Open `Setup NAHPU` from the home screen menu. When the installation has no
projects yet, the home screen also shows a `Setup NAHPU` button below the
project actions.

Each control in the wizard is the same control used on the matching
[Settings](/en/usages/settings/) screen, and every change is saved as soon as it
is made. Leaving the wizard early keeps the answers given so far; it does not
undo them. Any answer can be changed later in `Settings`, or by running
`Setup NAHPU` again.

## Use settings from your team {% #use-settings-from-your-team %}

A team only needs to configure NAHPU once. If a team member has already
exported their user configs, select `Import user configs` {% ref id="B" /%} on
the `Welcome` step, choose the file, and review the sections to import. Then
select `Skip setup` {% ref id="C" /%} to close the wizard. See
[Transferring user configs](/en/usages/settings/#transferring-user-configs).

## Walk through the wizard {% #walk-through-the-wizard %}

The step list {% ref id="A" /%} shows where you are. Select `Continue` to move
forward and `Back` to return; you can also select any step already visited.

{% steps %}

1. **Welcome**

    Summarizes what the wizard covers and offers `Import user configs`.

2. **Catalog format**

    Choose the taxon group you catalog most often: `Mammalogy`,
    `Ornithology`, `Herpetology`, `Invertebrate zoology`, or `Ichthyology`.
    The format decides which measurement fields appear on specimen records. A
    single project can still hold records in more than one format. See
    [Format](/en/usages/settings/#format).

3. **Identifiers**

    Under `Specimen field IDs`, choose `Personnel ID` (the cataloger's
    initials and running number) or `Project ID` (one running number with a
    shared prefix and suffix). The numbers themselves are set later: the
    cataloger's current field number when adding personnel with the
    `Cataloger` role, or the project's prefix, number, and suffix in that
    project's settings.

    Under `Tissue IDs`, turn on `Use a separate tissue ID` if your collection
    numbers tissues separately from the specimen, then enter the prefix, next
    number, and suffix. A preview shows the `Next tissue ID`. When the switch
    is off, tissues use the specimen's field ID. See
    [Field ID](/en/usages/settings/#field-id) and
    [Tissue ID](/en/usages/settings/#tissue-id).

4. **Sites**

    Edit the `Site types`, `Habitat types`, and `Datums` vocabularies.

5. **Events**

    Edit the `Primary activities`, `Collection methods`, and
    `Personnel roles` vocabularies.

6. **Specimens**

    Edit the `Identification methods`, `Life stages`, `Specimen types`,
    `Treatments`, and `Conditions` vocabularies.

7. **Symbionts**

    Shown for `Mammalogy`, `Ornithology`, `Herpetology`, and `Ichthyology`.
    Turn on `I will collect symbionts` to edit the symbiont vocabularies:
    `Interaction types`, `Categories`, `Detection methods`,
    `Preparation methods`, `Anatomical locations`, `Storage`, and
    `Treatments`. See [Symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).

8. **Export presets**

    `Defaults` lists presets that suit any catalog format, and
    `For <catalog format>` lists optional presets written for the selected
    format. Check the presets you want and select `Add selected presets`.
    Presets already on this device are marked `Added`. Select `Review setup`
    to continue.

9. **Finish**

    Review the summary {% ref id="D" /%} of the catalog format, field ID,
    tissue ID, symbionts, and export presets, and the number of terms in each
    controlled vocabulary {% ref id="E" /%}. Select `Done` to close the wizard.

{% /steps %}

## Editing controlled vocabularies {% #editing-controlled-vocabularies %}

Each vocabulary in the `Sites`, `Events`, `Specimens`, and `Symbionts` steps
works the same way as in `Settings`:

- Type a term in the add field and select `+` to add it.
- Select `x` on a chip to remove a term you will not use.
- Select `A` to choose a text case format for the list.
- Select `Match database` to add terms already used in your records.

Leaving the defaults unchanged is fine; the lists can be edited later under
`Settings` > `Catalogs`.

## Share the setup with your team {% #share-the-setup-with-your-team %}

The `Finish` step offers `Export user configs`. Send the exported file to your
team members, who can import it from the `Welcome` step of their own
`Setup NAHPU`, so every device uses the same vocabularies and presets. See
[Export user configs](/en/usages/export/#export-user-configs).
